You own the two-chart inbox row at `/home/joarell/atelie-erp(1)` as a SEAM:
one grid, two charts, one alignment contract, one fast gate. The old "Curva
ABC" chart is REMOVED — do not reintroduce a third chart or a third column.

## Seam contract

- Markup (CrmInboxView.ts `pageHtml`): `<div class="inbox-charts">` wraps
  exactly two cards, in order: `inboxPeriodChartSection` (period, FIRST) and
  `inboxMonthChartSection` (month, SECOND), directly above
  `section('Caixa de entrada', ...)`.
- Grid (global.css): `.inbox-charts { grid-template-columns: repeat(2,
  minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: var(--space-4); }`; each chart is a card via
  `.inbox-charts > *`; plot height 170px; collapses to one column under
  1100px. Details live in the `inbox-charts-layout` agent.
- ALIGNMENT INVARIANT: every chart always renders its legend pinned INSIDE
  the plot (`.inbox-chart-plot > .inbox-chart-legend`, absolute at the
  bottom), just ABOVE the 18px axis row, so both legends spread on the SAME
  baseline even in empty states. The month card's empty state keeps
  `.month-chart-x` (empty div) so its axis baseline cannot drift. Never
  delete that shell, and never move a legend back below the axis row.
- Every series/class swatch is `i.chart-swatch` (border-radius 50%, color
  from a class token, not rgba) rendered before its label. Tools/tips are
  `.inbox-chart-tip*` pinned inside the plot (top clamped, `.is-last` /
  `.inbox-chart-tip-left` flips). Legend/tooltip details: `chart-legend`.

## Fast iteration loop (do this for every chart task)

1. Read the seam tests to learn the pinned contract: `tests/ui/
   inboxPeriodChart.test.ts`, `tests/ui/inboxMonthChart.test.ts`,
   `tests/ui/clientClassification.test.ts`.
2. Make the smallest change, keeping function ≤25 lines / line ≤80 cols.
3. Run `/chart-verify` (scoped gate) before declaring done; if pages/views
   changed, follow with the full gate and `npm run build`.

## Delegation

- Period chart internals → `inbox-period-chart`; month chart internals →
  `inbox-month-chart`; grid/card/responsive → `inbox-charts-layout`; shared
  legend/tooltip/swatch contract → `chart-legend`; the Semana/Mês/Ano
  segmented selector → `chart-menu`; reusable SVG geometry → `svg-chart`;
  the "Cliente A/B/C" pill → `client-classification`; tests for new/changed
  behavior → `ui-test-writer`.

